WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.834
Okay, you ready?

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:03.962
♪

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.756
♪ Living in our high life ♪

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.677
♪ We're up on the high life ♪

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:14.806
The idea of the scene
should be that they're…

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:17.475
even though they're not
making it up as they go along,

00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:19.352
it should feel like
a live performance

00:00:19.436 --> 00:00:21.187
- Yeah.
- in a little pub in Dublin.

00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:24.858
I just love the idea
of little riffs that, like, felt like,

00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:28.069
"Okay, I can see a 
15-year-old kid doing that."

00:00:28.153 --> 00:00:29.988
-Yeah, yeah.
- So, it's nothing too complex.

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:31.448
So I just love that.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:37.662
(John singing with drum beat)

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:39.581
It's gotta be a marriage of…

00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:42.584
of creativity between a kid
who's on GarageBand

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:46.087
and who has beats,
with a girl who knows three chords.

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:49.424
Her contribution, guitar-wise,
has to be really simple.

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:51.468
And the audience have to go,
"I totally buy that."

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.845
I think there's notes that can
kind of hang through the chorus.

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:54.763
Like…

00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:57.223
♪

00:00:57.307 --> 00:01:00.643
♪ I'm not living in your life ♪

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.063
♪ You're not living in mine ♪

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:04.606
- You're saying keep four on the floor.
- Yeah.

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:06.441
- Is there a way to do that?
- ♪ Living the high life ♪

00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:10.236
♪ I'm a b*tch… 
but I'm your b*tch ♪

00:01:11.196 --> 00:01:12.947
"And… 
and I'm all you've got."

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:14.699
And she's kind of singing it
to the audience,

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:17.494
but she's also straining to speak to him,

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.454
and he's coming back to her.

00:01:19.537 --> 00:01:21.873
Now he can't, you know -
and won't - sing,

00:01:21.956 --> 00:01:23.541
so it would be kind of absurd,
in this movie,

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:25.502
if suddenly he was like…

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.504
Ed Sheeran or something, or singing out.

00:01:28.129 --> 00:01:30.090
Being the kid he is,
living in the flats

00:01:30.173 --> 00:01:32.008
and hanging out
with the guys doing drill,

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.843
he might do a little rap.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:34.844
So, I've been trying to write

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.639
from the point of view
of a 14-year-old Dublin boy.

00:01:38.223 --> 00:01:40.809
- Well, you once were.
- And this is my best effort.

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:44.020
This isn't my dumbing down
to try and get into his head.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.647
This is the best rap I can do.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:46.773
♪ Woman ♪

00:01:46.856 --> 00:01:48.483
♪ Guess we're cut from the same cloth ♪

00:01:48.566 --> 00:01:50.401
♪ Fourteen years on the same block ♪

00:01:50.485 --> 00:01:51.903
♪ Nine long months in your belly ♪

00:01:51.986 --> 00:01:53.905
♪ Down to the coom,
I still wasn't ready.

00:01:53.988 --> 00:01:55.907
♪ Three days late,
I arrive at the party ♪

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.826
♪ Smile on my face,
You're welcome, me hearty ♪

00:01:57.909 --> 00:01:59.202
Give me the bit just before that.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.703
Um, so it would be…

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.914
♪ Girl, we're cut from the same cloth ♪

00:02:02.997 --> 00:02:04.874
♪ Everything you feel,
I feel the same loss ♪

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.376
♪ I see your eyes in the mirror ♪

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.670
♪ Saint, angel, devil, sinner ♪

00:02:08.753 --> 00:02:10.004
Then I don't have anything else.

00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:14.342
(John singing)

00:02:14.425 --> 00:02:16.469
♪ Still here in the high life ♪

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:18.304
Bang! And she's like,
"F*ckin' hell!"

00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:19.848
You know, so if he's saying,

00:02:20.265 --> 00:02:23.768
"What I've realized at the end of all this
is actually we're dead similar."

00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:25.520
- It's actually weirdly moving.
- Yes.

00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:27.063
- Do you know what I mean?
- I actually think it can be.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.398
For a second you think it's funny,

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.359
and then it, like, hits you
with a killer emotional line.

00:02:31.442 --> 00:02:33.486
♪ We're living the high life ♪

00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:37.824
♪ Living in our high life ♪

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:41.161
♪ We're up on the high life ♪

00:02:42.954 --> 00:02:46.249
♪ And it's a fine night to feel alive ♪

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.501
♪ We're living the high life ♪
(audience clapping along with music)

